cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "llama-annotation-pipeline: Snakemake workflow and documented commands for homology-based and ab initio annotation of the Lama glama genome"
abstract: >-
  Workflow, environment definitions and helper scripts used to annotate the
  protein-coding gene complement of a Lama glama genome assembly
  (GCA_028534125.1) by four strategies, and to benchmark the resulting
  proteomes. Three homology strategies project the Vicugna pacos reference
  annotation (GCF_048564905.1): DNA-to-DNA lift-over (Liftoff),
  protein-to-genome alignment (miniprot) and hybrid reconciliation (LiftOn).
  The fourth strategy is reference-independent ab initio prediction (Helixer).
  Proteomes are evaluated with BUSCO, with structural statistics from AGAT and
  concordance from gffcompare. The Snakemake workflow automates data
  acquisition, the Liftoff and miniprot branches and their quality control; the
  LiftOn and Helixer branches were run manually and on external GPU
  infrastructure respectively, with the exact commands documented in
  REPRODUCIBILITY.md.
